        "title": "Prefer OpenCode Go local usage in Auto mode",
        "body": "## Summary\n- prefer OpenCode Go local history before the web fetch in Auto mode\n- keep explicit Web source web-only, and keep web fallback when local history is unavailable\n- update strategy tests for the new order and fallback contract\n\n## Why\nThe OpenCode Go timing reported in #2117 shows `codexbar usage --provider opencodego` spending about 20 seconds. Auto currently runs the web strategy first, so a slow or missing web session can delay the fast local SQLite reader even when local history can satisfy the usage display.\n\n## Tests\n- `swiftc -parse Sources/CodexBarCore/Providers/OpenCodeGo/OpenCodeGoProviderDescriptor.swift`\n- `swiftc -parse Tests/CodexBarTests/OpenCodeGoProviderStrategyTests.swift`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `swift test --filter OpenCodeGoProviderStrategyTests`\n- `make check`\n\n## Compatibility risk\nLow. This changes only OpenCode Go Auto strategy precedence; `--source web` still uses the web strategy directly, and Auto still falls through to web when local history is missing or unreadable.",
